---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Default.astro';
import StoreButtons from '../../components/StoreButtons.astro';
import apps from '../../data/staff_apps.json';
import site from '../../data/config.json';
const arbiter = apps.find((app) => app.slug === 'arbiter');
---
<Layout title="Safety" description="How AudienceKit keeps communities safe: member reports and automatic checks flag problems, Arbiter's AI host helps in chat, and the people who know your community make every call that matters." image="/assets/brand/arbiter.png">

<section class="section wrap scene sov-hero" aria-labelledby="safety-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Safety on AudienceKit</p>
    <h1 id="safety-title">Big-platform safety.<br><em>Your people decide.</em></h1>
  </div>
  <div class="scene-copy">
    <p class="large-copy">Machines flag. People make the calls that matter.</p>
    <p>The tools that keep the largest platforms safe usually need a trust and safety department to run. AudienceKit brings them to communities of every size: reports and automatic checks catch problems as they appear, an AI host helps in chat, and anything serious waits for someone from your own team.</p>
    <p>That someone works in <a href="#arbiter">Arbiter</a>, our moderation app for iPhone, iPad and Mac.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section capabilities" id="layers" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How a problem is handled</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="layers-title">Flag, help, decide</h2>
      <p class="capability-intro">Each layer hands what it can’t settle to the next, and the last one is always a person.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid steps">
      <div class="capability-card step">
        <div class="step__num" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3>Automated tools flag</h3>
        <p>Member reports, blocks, automatic message checks and your own word lists catch problems the moment they appear, so nobody has to watch every room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-card step">
        <div class="step__num" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3>An AI host helps</h3>
        <p>Where an audience turns it on, Arbiter’s AI host reads venue chat as it happens, answers questions, handles the small stuff with a private nudge, and proposes what to do about the rest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-card step">
        <div class="step__num" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3>People decide</h3>
        <p>Anything the AI isn’t sure of, and anything punitive, waits for a person in Arbiter’s queue. Every action is logged and can be undone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap arbiter" id="arbiter" aria-labelledby="arbiter-title">
  <div class="arbiter-art"><img src={'/assets/brand/arbiter.png'} width="1254" height="1254" alt="Arbiter's gold balance scale with glowing glass pans" loading="lazy"></div>
  <div class="arbiter-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Arbiter · iPhone, iPad &amp; Mac</p>
    <h2 id="arbiter-title">The calls the AI<br>shouldn’t make alone.</h2>
    <p class="large-copy">Arbiter is where your administrators review what AudienceKit’s AI decided, and decide what it couldn’t.</p>
    <p>AudienceKit’s AI handles routine work on its own: listing suggestions, research on submissions and moderation calls. Arbiter shows your team the rest, in three lists that stay live as people work:</p>
    <ul class="sov-list">
      <li><strong>Needs you.</strong> What the AI wasn’t sure of, couldn’t answer, or isn’t allowed to decide alone, the least certain first.</li>
      <li><strong>Decided by AI.</strong> What it was confident about and applied on its own, so you can check its work.</li>
      <li><strong>Decided by people.</strong> What your team decided, and whether they went the AI’s way.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each decision shows the AI’s answer with a probability for every option, its reasoning and evidence, and the options it couldn’t rule out. For a suggested listing change, every field it would change sits beside the listing as it is now. One person can look after several audiences from the same app.</p>
    {arbiter && <StoreButtons app={arbiter} />}
    <p class="arbiter-note">Arbiter needs an AudienceKit account with administrator access to an audience. Sign in with Apple or Facebook. Share <a class="text-link" href={'/apps/arbiter/'}>audiencekit.com/apps/arbiter</a> with your team.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section capabilities" id="ai-host" aria-labelledby="host-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The AI host, on your own Mac</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="host-title">An AI host with guard rails</h2>
      <p class="capability-intro">On a Mac, Arbiter can do the work itself: it runs the audience’s decision worker and the AI host for venue chats on models stored on that Mac, so those messages aren’t sent to a third-party AI service.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12s3-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-3 7-10 7-10-7-10-7Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="m3 3 18 18"/></svg></div>
        <h3>It never knows who’s talking</h3>
        <p>The host reads the conversation with people replaced by letters. It never gets a member’s name, profile or tribes, and it only acts on messages from the live chat.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Code sets the limits, not the model</h3>
        <p>Whatever the model suggests, a fixed set of rules decides what may happen. Punitive calls always wait for a person, nothing targets staff, the venue or its hosts, and the host won’t chime in unasked more than once every two minutes in a room.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 8v4l3 3"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Automated bans don’t stick on their own</h3>
        <p>A ban proposed by automation goes to your staff straight away and lasts 24 hours at most unless one of your team confirms it. Every action is recorded with its reason and can be undone.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 21v-7M4 10V3M12 21v-9M12 8V3M20 21v-5M20 12V3M1 14h6M9 8h6M17 16h6"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Start in shadow</h3>
        <p>The host starts in shadow mode, where it carries nothing out and your team can judge each call it would have made. Move to approving every call, then to live, when you trust it. Each audience sets its own guidelines and thresholds in the admin console.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Honest about what it is</h3>
        <p>Asked, the host says it’s an AI and which model it runs. It answers from the chat and the venue’s own listings, and doesn’t invent events.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Your team sees its work</h3>
        <p>Every call the host makes is uploaded for review, with what it read and why it chose what it did. Anyone on your team can look from an iPhone or iPad without running a model.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section capabilities" id="more" aria-labelledby="more-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the chat</p>
      <h2 class="capability-title" id="more-title">Safety on the floor and in every upload</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2v4M12 18v4M4.9 4.9l2.8 2.8M16.3 16.3l2.8 2.8M2 12h4M18 12h4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Help on the floor</h3>
        <p>A guest who feels unsafe at a venue taps once, and the staff on shift hear it on their devices straight away in <a href={'/apps/velvet/'}>Velvet</a>. One of them picks it up, the guest is told who is coming, and alerts nobody answers go up to the managers.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10Z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Child safety</h3>
        <p>Images are checked only against lists of known child sexual abuse material, never guessed at by a classifier. A match or a member’s report withholds the content at once and opens a case for a trained reviewer, and a person files every report to NCMEC’s CyberTipline. Read the <a href={'/child-safety/'}>Child Safety &amp; CSAM Policy</a>.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <div class="feature__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Your rules, your dials</h3>
        <p>Automated moderation is something an audience turns on, not a default. Each audience sets its own guidelines and chooses how bold the host may be. What’s banter in one scene is a problem in another, so the community sets the line.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="large-copy" style="margin-top:44px;max-width:62ch">See every safety tool on the <a href={'/integrations/#safety'} style="text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px">integrations menu</a>. To report a problem, use <strong>Report</strong> in the app, or write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact_email}?subject=Safety%20report`} style="text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px">{site.contact_email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap closing" aria-labelledby="safety-closing-title"><p class="eyebrow">Your community, your call.</p><h2 id="safety-closing-title">Keep your scene<br><em>safe and yours.</em></h2><p>Tell us about the community you look after.<br>We’ll help you set up its rules and its host.</p><a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${site.contact_email}?subject=Safety%20on%20AudienceKit`}>Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .sov-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(52px, 7vw, 88px); line-height: .98; }
  .scene-copy p + p { margin-top: 18px; }
  .scene-copy a, .capability-card p a, .arbiter-copy > p a:not(.text-link) { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .arbiter { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  .arbiter-art img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 22%; }
  .arbiter-copy h2 { margin-top: 10px; }
  .arbiter-copy > p, .arbiter-copy > ul { margin-top: 18px; max-width: 62ch; }
  .sov-list { padding-left: 1.2em; color: var(--muted); display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .sov-list strong { color: var(--paper); }
  .arbiter-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .arbiter { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .arbiter-art { max-width: 220px; }
  }
</style>
